- WORKER TCB FINDING: cycle 2 binds the launcher, interpreter binary/link chain, and installed `site-packages/csk` tree, but launches the ordinary Python console script with `site` startup enabled. A fresh wheel-installed venv accepted a real native Go build while an executable sibling `.pth` hook ran before `csk.cli`; mutating that hook did not change the manager identity digest. The worker's complete mutable startup TCB is therefore still not identity-bound.
- NATIVE-PROBE FINDING: macOS inventory entries statically marked unavailable bypass `_native_probe`; only 3 of 5 controls were genuinely probed, while all five evidence entries claimed `probed_at=pre-worker-launch`. The rc.5 per-operation rule excludes a host label or build-time constant from being an availability probe.
- GATE ANOMALY: the authoritative focused run failed 1 of 178 cases because `manager-package-replaced-after-launch` returned `build_execution_control_unavailable` instead of `build_execution_worker_identity_invalid`; the case then passed 10 isolated runs and the full suite passed 861 / skipped 6, demonstrating an order-sensitive or nondeterministic diagnostic boundary. Strict mypy and hygiene remained green.
- VERDICT: changes requested; route `to-dev`. Evidence and required rework are recorded in `TASK-260720-2g21eg_review-verdict-cycle-2.md`.

### 2026-07-30 — Protected POSIX cache Linux quarantine CI rework
- TRIGGER: CocoaSkills PR #11 CI run `30514706010` passed strict mypy plus every macOS and Windows test job, but all four Ubuntu versions failed the same four cache tests at `_move_aside` with `PermissionError: [Errno 13]`.
- ROOT CAUSE: the verified temporary owner-unlock path was gated to Darwin. Linux therefore attempted ordinary quarantine rename with sealed directory modes `0500`, `0550`, or `0000`; owner write/execute control was absent at the rename boundary.
- FIX: the existing rooted, no-follow, effective-UID and inode-verified unlock now applies to owned POSIX directories generally, skips mutation only when full owner `rwx` is already present, and restores the exact original mode after both successful and failed rename.
- REGRESSION: Linux-semantic seams force `EACCES` unless the candidate has temporary owner control, cover sealed `0500`, untrusted `0550`, and inaccessible `0000`, and prove exact mode restoration plus reservation cleanup when rename itself fails.
- GATES: the test-first reproducer exited 1 as expected; final POSIX-focused pytest exited 0 with 37 passed; full accepted-root pytest exited 0 with 886 passed / 6 skipped; strict mypy passed 63 source files; diff hygiene, compileall, distribution build, and Twine metadata all exited 0.
- EVIDENCE: board outcome `TASK-260720-2jfnz6_linux-ci-rework.md`; the task branch remains unstaged/uncommitted for the commit-owning mover and requires a fresh Ubuntu matrix after integration.

### 2026-07-30 — Fixed go-v1 compile-driver cycle-3 review finds unbound runtime code and a user-selectable hidden mode
- REVIEWER: `TASK-260720-2g21eg` cycle 3 on CocoaSkills base `495ad021847529ce5a544dba415ca2fe19949539`; clean local `main`, `main`, and `origin/main` matched, both dependency tasks were accepted, and the four candidate hashes matched the producer packet. No CocoaSkills source or test file was modified.
- RUNTIME-TCB FINDING: the cycle-3 startup identity hashes selected immediate startup hooks and records only the standard-library root inode/mode. Ordinary importable standard-library files are neither identity entries nor retained watch paths, while `validate_worker_runtime` accepts any loaded module path below that root without a content identity. An isolated probe changed the bytes of the worker-imported `json/__init__.py`; manager/startup identity remained equal, the macOS mutation guard closed without an event, and both pre/post runtime proofs were accepted. Mutable Python code can therefore execute before the ready proof without `build_execution_worker_identity_invalid`, leaving the mandatory worker identity and pre/post re-verification boundary open.
- HIDDEN-MODE FINDING: `cli.main()` checks actual `sys.argv` for `__csk-go-worker-v1` before the public parser. Invoking the installed entry point directly as `csk __csk-go-worker-v1 </dev/null` selected `run_worker`, returned its length-framed worker-protocol failure, and exited 3. The test rejects only programmatic `cli.main([mode])` while explicitly accepting the actual external-CLI path, contrary to the rc.5 requirement that the hidden mode is not a user-visible command surface and no user option selects it.
- GREEN GATES: accepted-root focused pytest passed 289 / skipped 4; full pytest passed 962 / skipped 6; the separate wheel-installed native macOS Go fixture passed all 6 scenarios; strict mypy passed 62 source files; tabnanny, trailing-whitespace, and diff hygiene passed. Green regression gates do not cover either reproduced boundary.
- VERDICT: changes requested; route `to-dev`. Evidence and exact rework requirements are in `TASK-260720-2g21eg_review-verdict-cycle-3.md` plus the attached standard-library and hidden-mode probes.

